  <h1>Reports that help readers find the meaning<span class="red-stop">.</span></h1>
  <p class="page-lede">We turn research, evaluation and specialist material into visual reports and summaries that are credible, navigable and useful to readers with different levels of time and expertise.</p>
</header>

<section class="service-page-intro">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">Visual report design</p><h2>Make a long document easier to enter, understand and use.</h2></div>
  <div class="prose"><p>A report can contain excellent evidence and still make its central findings difficult to locate. We work with the content as well as the page: establishing hierarchy, separating the main narrative from supporting detail and deciding where a visual explanation will do more than prose.</p><p>The result may be a complete publication, an executive summary or a connected family of outputs for different audiences. The objective is not to remove necessary complexity, but to give every reader a clearer route through it.</p></div>
</section>

<section class="section-shell service-offers">
  <div class="split-heading"><h2>Designed for evidence-rich communication<span class="red-stop">.</span></h2><p>We create documents that work for close reading, quick orientation and practical dissemination.</p></div>
  <div class="service-offer-grid">
    <article><span>01</span><h3>Research reports</h3><p>Clear editorial structures for findings, methods, evidence and recommendations without flattening the argument.</p></article>
    <article><span>02</span><h3>Evaluation and impact</h3><p>Reports that connect activity, evidence and outcomes for funders, partners and programme teams.</p></article>
    <article><span>03</span><h3>Executive summaries</h3><p>Shorter resources designed around the decisions and findings a time-poor audience needs first.</p></article>
    <article><span>04</span><h3>Briefing publications</h3><p>Focused documents that make policy, technical or organisational material easier to discuss and act on.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="service-practical">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">What the work can include</p><h2>A coherent system for words, evidence and visuals.</h2></div>
  <ul class="service-checklist"><li>Information architecture and content hierarchy</li><li>Page planning and editorial pacing</li><li>Charts, tables, diagrams and pull-outs</li><li>Executive summaries and visual overviews</li><li>Accessible digital and print-ready files</li><li>Templates and coordinated publication assets</li></ul>
</section>

